course: dictionary
lesson: 13829
title: The travel itinerary
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An itinerary is a plan of a journey. It lists the places you will visit and the times you will be at each one. When you meet a new word, read the words around it. «Our itinerary says we leave the hotel at 8:30 and reach the museum at 10:00.» The places and the times are the clues.
explain: Look for the signs of an itinerary: place names, times, and the order they come in. «First the train to Bath, then a walk to the abbey, then lunch at noon.» Each stop comes in order, like a list. Check your meaning by swapping it in: "a plan of the journey" fits the sentence, so you are right.
explain: Itinerary is a noun, and it often goes with travel: a travel itinerary, or a school trip itinerary. In maths, an itinerary helps you work out how long a trip takes. If the bus leaves at 9:15 and arrives at 11:05, the gap between those two times is the journey time.
fact: An itinerary is a plan of a journey.
fact: An itinerary lists the places to visit and the times.
fact: «Itinerary» is a noun: one itinerary, many itineraries.
fact: A travel itinerary is the plan for a trip.
fact: To find the journey time on an itinerary, work out the gap between the start time and the arrival time.
exercise: «Our itinerary says we leave the hotel at 8:30.» What is an itinerary? | *A plan of a journey, listing places and times | A type of bus | A map of the ocean floor | A bag for packing clothes
exercise: «Dad read the itinerary aloud: first the ferry, then the castle.» Find and copy the word that means a plan of a journey. | castle | aloud | ferry | *itinerary
exercise: «The itinerary shows the bus leaves at 9:15 and reaches the town at 11:05.» How long is the bus journey? | 20 minutes | 1 hour 10 minutes | 2 hours 10 minutes | *1 hour 50 minutes
test: What is the plural of itinerary? | itinerary's | *itineraries | itinerarys | itinerarium
test: In a travel itinerary, what does the list of times tell you? | The colour of the bus | The name of the driver | *When to be at each place | How many sweets to pack
exam: «The itinerary shows we arrive in Rome at 14:30 and leave at 16:00.» How long do we stay in Rome? | 1 hour 00 minutes | *1 hour 30 minutes | 2 hours 30 minutes | 30 minutes
